93 ng/L at 3 hours; electrocardiogram showed normal sinus rhythm without ST-T changes. \n\nHis home medications included insulin glargine 18 units nightly, insulin aspart 5 units before each meal, and empagliflozin started one month earlier.", "frontier": ["FLAT"], "root": {"alarm_features": ["Hypotension", "Severe metabolic acidosis", "Acute renal failure", "Dehydration"], "confidence": 0.8, "excluded_candidates": ["Diabetic ketoacidosis: while the patient has type 2 diabetes and elevated β-hydroxybutyrate, the primary issue appears to be severe metabolic acidosis and acute renal failure rather than diabetic ketoacidosis alone", "Septic shock: there is no clear evidence of infection or sepsis, and the patient's presentation is more consistent with severe metabolic acidosis and acute renal failure"], "label": "Acute Renal Failure with Severe Metabolic Acidosis and Hypotension", "salient_findings": ["Severe metabolic acidosis", "Acute renal failure", "Hypotension", "Elevated lactate level", "Elevated β-hydroxybutyrate level", "Dehydration", "Sarcopenia"], "severity": "unspecified", "supporting_facts": ["Decreased oral intake and dehydration for at least one week", "Hypotension (blood pressure 94/49 mmHg and 101/59 mmHg)", "Severe metabolic acidosis (venous pH 7.09, anion gap 31, bicarbonate 8 mEq/L)", "Acute renal failure (creatinine 10.2 mg/dL, baseline 1.1 mg/dL)", "Elevated lactate (4.4 mmol/L) and β-hydroxybutyrate (31.5 mmol/L) levels"], "time_course": "acute"}, "static_evidence_items": [{"branch_links": {}, "content": "Demographics: 74-year-old man", "id": "E1", "independent": true, "kind": "direct", "metadata": {"extractor": "diagnosisarena_vignette_parser_freeze_v2"}, "source_ids": []}, {"branch_links": {}, "content": "Medical history: type 2 diabetes mellitus", "id": "E2", "independent": true, "kind": "direct", "metadata": {"extractor": "diagnosisarena_vignette_parser_freeze_v2"}, "source_ids": []}, {"branch_links": {}, "content": "Medical history: hypertens